{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Be stupefied.</b> He speaks about [emendation: read אל] the people of Zion, that they should be dumbfounded to investigate how this can be, and what is the secret of this prophecy. And behold, the prophet speaks as a man speaks to his fellow, and why do they not know that they are drunk, but not from wine:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads על [צ\"ל אל], a scribal correction notation indicating על should read אל; I preserved both the original and the emendation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:47.059976198Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}